# Jira GRW-420 — the build context for THIS repo's Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` before falling back to a
# context-root `.dockerignore`, so this is the file that applies to
# `docker build -f Dockerfile .` here.
#
# What was here before was the monorepo's copy, and every path in it was one
# level too deep: it excluded `web/node_modules`, `web/.next` and
# `web/**/*.test.ts`, none of which exist in this repository — while leaving
# this repo's OWN `.next` and test files in the context. A stale local `.next`
# copied into the build is the kind of thing that produces a working image on
# one laptop and a broken one on another.

# Never ship a local install or a local build into the context.
node_modules
.next
out

# Version control and CI.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Editor and tooling noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log

# Local secrets and environment. None of these should exist here, and if one
# ever does it must not reach an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tests do not belong in a runtime image. `next build` does not read them, and
# they are a third of the files in app/.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx

# The image is built from source, not from a previous image's output.
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.dockerignore
